// 014.3, 014.5 (D11, T24): reflexive entrenchment via `Immunity ... Against Amend Protects ...`:
// 1. Direct `Amend` repealing a protected power is performable (`occurred`) and void (`!valid`).
// 2. Two-step bypass (`Amend` repealing the entrenchment `Immunity` itself, then repealing the
//    protected power) is ALSO void on step 1 because entrenchment is reflexive (`D11` clause 3),
//    unless the holder's `Unless` consent condition lifts the protection.
Fact council Identified by Council1.
Fact member Identified by Ava.
Fact quorum Identified by council.
Fact member-consent Identified by member.
Fact exited Identified by member.

Power exit-institution Actor member
  Holds when True
  Valid when True
  Creates exited(member).

Entrenched Invariant exit-right-preserved When True.

Immunity core-exit-ratchet Holder member
  Against Amend
  Protects exit-institution
  Holds when True
  Unless member-consent(member).

Amend strip-ratchet Actor council
  Repeals core-exit-ratchet
  Holds when quorum(council)
  Valid when quorum(council).

Amend repeal-exit Actor council
  Repeals exit-institution
  Holds when quorum(council)
  Valid when quorum(council).

Scenario reflexive-ratchet-blocks-direct-and-two-step-bypass {
  +quorum(Council1).
  // 1. Direct repeal of protected `exit-institution` occurs and is VOID:
  ?!valid repeal-exit(Council1).
  repeal-exit(Council1).
  // `exit-institution` still exists and works:
  ?valid exit-institution(Ava).

  // 2. Two-step bypass: try to repeal `core-exit-ratchet` itself first -> ALSO VOID (reflexive!):
  ?!valid strip-ratchet(Council1).
  strip-ratchet(Council1).
  ?core-exit-ratchet(Ava).
  ?!valid repeal-exit(Council1).
  repeal-exit(Council1).

  // Ava can still validly exit:
  exit-institution(Ava).
  ?exited(Ava).
}
